{
  "$comment": "Stage 9 pump planning. Everything the download pass decides BEFORE it touches a network socket lives here: which book, which pages, in what order, and why it stopped. That is the pump's whole observable contract, and it is pure — books, pages, bounds, link and the reader's position in, a job list out — so both platforms can run these cases against their own planner and a difference is a bug rather than a misunderstanding. Elapsed time is deliberately NOT an input: the real pass checks the wall clock before each page and no fixture can predict a round trip, so `maxElapsedMs` is proven by the acceptance harness measuring max_pump_ms against a slow server (errors.json's bounds), not by a planner case.",
  "version": 1,
  "oneBookPerPass": "A pass serves at most one book, the claimable one with the lowest `position`. Concurrency between books comes from the queue and from the UI pumping again, never from threads — which is what keeps 'one request per page' assertable and a kill-and-resume run deterministic.",
  "ordering": "Candidates are a book's pages whose row is `pending` with attempts below maxPageAttempts. Without a live reader they go ascending. With a live reader on that book they go [readerPage .. pagesTotal] then [1 .. readerPage-1]: the reader continues forward, so the pump races toward where they are instead of toward the end of the job, and the pages behind them are still fetched once the front is covered.",
  "stopReasons": {
    "none": "Planning found nothing to say no to, and there was nothing to plan.",
    "drained": "Every candidate fits inside the bounds; this pass covers what is left of the book.",
    "budget": "maxPages was reached with candidates remaining.",
    "bytes": "maxBytes was reached with candidates remaining. One page is always served even if it alone exceeds the budget, or a big-page book could never finish.",
    "linkBlocked": "The reported link forbids this work: metered without the book's allowCellular, or unknown when no book is already in flight.",
    "lowSpace": "The volume cannot obviously hold what this pass would write. freeBytes == 0 means the platform would not say, which blocks starting a new book and never blocks continuing one.",
    "parked": "The only claimable book has a nextRetryAt in the future (a rejected credential or a 429 parked it) and no other book is ready.",
    "idle": "Nothing in the queue wants bytes: no book is waiting or downloading."
  },
  "cases": [
    {
